ucky district that leans Republican by about seven points. Republican Ralph Alvarado, a former state senator with name recognition from statewide runs, faces Democrat Zach Dembo, an attorney who has kept pace financially, with both campaigns aided by heavy outside spending from national PACs tied to Trump and Gov. Andy Beshear.\n\nRatings split between Lean R and Likely R, and Democratic-sponsored polls from mid-summer showed the race essentially tied, though partisan sponsorship and small samples warrant caution. Prediction markets still favor the Republican by a wide margin. The forecast expects a narrow but real Republican edge, with genuine Democratic upside if the affordability message and Beshear's popularity travel well in the Lexington media market.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2515, "margin": -3.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.296, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2877, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2982, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2389, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2735, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2956, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2849, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3514, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3215, "margin": -3.5}]}